    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0361" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg291"/>

                <head>No. 147.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Morton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 13,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 379.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information a copy of
                    Mr. Schuyler’s dispatch, dated the 19th ultimo, and its accompaniment,
                    respecting the prohibition <pb facs="0362" n="292" xml:id="pg292"/> by the
                    Hellenic Government of pork products coming from America, adding, what will be
                    particularly noted by you, that Greece otters, no reason for this action save
                    the precedent established by France.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
